      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-22-2025-june/q1",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:110mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-22-2025-june/q01-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. Speed-time graph for a runner travelling from A to B.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a sketch of the speed-time graph for a model of the motion of a runner travelling along a straight horizontal road from a point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> to a point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>.</p><p>The distance from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> is 400 metres.</p><p>In the model of the motion, the runner</p><ul><li>starts from rest at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t = 0\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>then moves with constant acceleration for 5 seconds, reaching a maximum speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5 \\text{ m s}^{-1}\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>then travels at a constant speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5 \\text{ m s}^{-1}\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>then moves with constant deceleration for 15 seconds, until coming to rest at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>travels from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> seconds</li></ul><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) State one reason why the actual time taken to travel from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> might not be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> seconds.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
