      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-22-2025-june/q2",
      "question": "<p>A particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> has mass 0.25 kg.</p><p>The particle moves on a smooth horizontal surface under the action of two horizontal forces <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf F_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf F_2\"></span></p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf F_1 = (3\\mathbf i - 5\\mathbf j)N\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf F_2 = (-6\\mathbf i + 9\\mathbf j)N\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) find, in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf i\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf j\"></span>, the resultant force acting on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>,</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) find the magnitude of the acceleration of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>A third horizontal force, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf F_3\"></span>, is now applied to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p><p>Under the action of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf F_1\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf F_2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf F_3\"></span>, the particle moves with constant velocity.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf F_3\"></span>, giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf i\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf j\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
